course: dictionary
lesson: 4415
title: Halt: to stop, or a stop
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Halt is a short word with a clear job: it means to stop, or to make something stop. «The rain halted the match.» The match stopped, so halted must mean stopped. Try the meaning in the sentence to check it.
explain: Halt can also be a noun, meaning a stop. «The cars came to a halt at the red light.» Come to a halt means the cars stopped. «Britain grinds to a halt» means the whole country slows down until it stops. Grind to a halt is a slow stop, like a heavy bus wheezing to a stop.
explain: Sometimes halt is a shout. In stories a guard calls, «Halt! Who goes there?» The guard is asking who is coming, so the person must stop at once. The context tells you the meaning.
fact: Halt means to stop, or to make something stop.
fact: As a noun, a halt is a stop: «come to a halt».
fact: «Halt!» is an order to stop at once, often shouted by soldiers or guards.
fact: «Grind to a halt» means to slow down and stop gradually.
fact: Check a new word by swapping in a meaning: «The rain halted the match» still makes sense with stopped.
exercise: «The rain halted the match.» What does halted mean here? | *Stopped | Started | Painted | Cheered
exercise: «The cars came to a halt at the red light.» What does a halt mean? | A bright light | *A stop | A loud noise | A race
exercise: A guard shouts, «Halt! Who goes there?» What should the person do? | *Stop at once | Ask for a drink | Run away fast | Sing a song
test: «Work came to a halt when the power failed.» What does came to a halt mean? | *Stopped | Sped up | Got louder | Painted the walls
test: Which word means to stop? | *halt | happy | hello | hallway
exam: «The guard shouted, "Halt!"» What does halt mean here? | *Stop at once | Look up | Wave hello | Sit down
